																		A Parasitic Crystal (Reanimation SCP) - Seeking Greenlights
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/harvoable" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(7005588); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=7005588&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1605818720" alt="Harvoable " style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=7005588)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/harvoable" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(7005588); return false;" >Harvoable </a></span> <span class="odate time_1605532729 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">16 Nov 2020 13:18</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4819947">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes.</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article.</p>
<p><strong>Genre (Optional):</strong> Horror (body/existential), mystery undertones.</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout (Optional):</strong> Classic SCP layout, with addendums, recovery and interview log.</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> 20 years ago, a seemingly un-ageing and charismatic man started a zealous cult in the rural United States. Through the years, he offered some of the more frail and elderly members of the cult an end to their angst, pain, and suffering through immortal life. However, there's a price: death, followed by reanimation. As time passes, it becomes apparant to those who declined his offer that reanimated individuals aren't the same as they were.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">▼&nbsp;Open&nbsp;me!</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">▲&nbsp;Close&nbsp;me!</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> The narrative takes place directly after the Foundation becomes aware of the cult. After a defector fled following the reanimation of his wife, he shared his story. Foundation drones equipped with thermal imaging cameras confirm that some of the members emit no body heat signature.</p>
<p>A recovery log details how MTF Psi-8 were dispatched to apprehend reanimated individuals, and were successful after armed resistance. The results confirmed the claims of the defector: many who were shot functioned long past what would otherwise prove fatal to a normal human.</p>
<p>What follows is a series of interviews, starting with the defector and his descriptions of the cult leader who seemingly didn't age a day in 20 years. The reason he fled was because his wife, dying of cancer, was persuaded by the charismatic leader, and took him up on his offer. However, what came back <em>wasn't</em> his wife. Nobody else could notice a difference, but he could; they'd been married for decades. Her strange behaviour escalated until she was begging for him to undergo the reanimation process.</p>
<p>Following interviews are with the cult leader. Many things he claims don't check out, and it's eventually discovered he is not who he says he is.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> There's more to the objects nature than researchers initially thought. Eventually, it is discovered that reanimated individuals are <em>not</em> the previously deceased, merely masquerading as them. The Crystal is sentient, and an entity inhabits it. It is anomalously impersonating dead individuals (as a hive-mind) in an attempt to convince those closest to them to undergo reanimation. It does this though promises of eternal life and an end to suffering. Who (or rather what) the entity is is eventually revealed. It's a demonic entity trapped within the Crystal, reduced to a parasite, feeding off life-energy to survive.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> Perhaps help with a better explanation for how the Foundation came to know about the existence of the cult.</p>
</div>
