<blockquote>
<p>This is where SCP-2718 comes in. The crystal uses its knowledge of the afterlife to horrify those it speaks to (via reanimated individuals). It offers them a choice: die conventionally, and you'll rot for all eternity in agonising pain or agree to be reanimated (in which case they will simply cease to exist, which is far less bleak in comparison).</p>
</blockquote>
<p>So, as a first time author I strongly suggest you do not center your anomaly in another well established, and well known, mainlist article. It often comes off as “I needed to root this idea to another to make it work.” I suggest finding some other reason why the crystal is animating bodies and impersonating the dead.</p>
<p>If you keep it vague why the crystal is doing this, and the article succeeds, then you could always write a tale later to expand and explore the context of SCP-2718.<br />
<span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span></p>
<blockquote>
<p>As for its history and origin of its anomalous abilities, I felt like explaining too much just negates the mystery.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Well, if this is true, then certainly going into the motivations of the entity violates the same “rule”.</p>
<p>I personally would be more interested in the history of the Crystal and the entity inhabiting it, than tying this all to another SCP.</p>

